data.value:
This software uses the SAE Z-DOWN axis system orientation:

- Positive lateral forces and accelerations point to the right;
- Positive longitudinal forces and accelerations point forward;
- Positive forces point downward;
- Positive yaw moment and yaw rate rotate the vehicle clockwise from a top view perspective;
- Positive roll angle (Ψ) lowers the right side of the vehicle;
- Positive pitch angle (Φ) lowers the rear of the vehicle;
- Positive chassis slip angle (β) and steering wheel angle (δd) point to the right;
- Positive tire slip angles (α) point to the right;
- Positive tire slip ratios (κ) and torques happen during traction (drive).
